## Technical Architecture

### Core Components

1. **Simulation Engine** (`spacecraft_simulation.py`)
   - Integrates Basilisk dynamics
   - Manages time propagation
   - Handles fault injection events
   - Cluster management integration
   - ML detection hooks

2. **GUI Framework** (`spacecraft_simulator_gui.py`)
   - Tkinter-based interface
   - Model-View pattern
   - Event-driven architecture
   - 9 specialized tabs (including new DRL tab)
   - Real-time status monitoring

3. **Fault System** (`fault_loader.py`)
   - Dynamic module loading
   - Plugin architecture for new fault types
   - Real-time fault injection
   - Cluster-wide fault propagation

4. **ML Detection System** (`real_ml_fault_detection.py`)
   - TensorFlow/Keras backend
   - Feature extraction pipeline
   - Real-time anomaly scoring
   - Fault type classification

5. **DRL System** (`drl_integration_bridge.py`, `drl_tab.py`)
   - PPO agent interface
   - Dedicated GUI tab for DRL management
   - State/action space management
   - Task redistribution logic
   - Safe mode fallback
   - Real-time performance monitoring

6. **Cluster Manager** (`cluster_integration.py`)
   - Formation geometry control
   - Leader-follower hierarchy
   - Inter-satellite communication
   - Formation quality metrics

7. **Visualization Pipeline**
   - Matplotlib for 2D plots
   - Vizard binary generation for 3D
   - Cluster-specific visualization
   - Formation geometry plots
   - DRL performance visualization

### Data Flow
```
User Input → GUI (9 Tabs) → Configuration → Simulation Engine
                                                 ↓
                                       Basilisk Dynamics
                                                 ↓
                                       Fault Injection
                                                 ↓
                                  ML Fault Detection (Real-Time)
                                                 ↓
                                  DRL Decision (via DRL Tab)
                                                 ↓
                                   Task Reassignment
                                                 ↓
Results ← Plotting Engine ← Data Recording ← Cluster Manager
       ← DRL Tab (Analysis)
```

### Integration Architecture
```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│           GUI Layer (Tkinter)               │
│  Constellation | Fault | Detection | DRL   │
│  DRL Tab | Tasks | Target | Viz | Output   │
└──────────────────┬──────────────────────────┘
                   │
┌──────────────────┴──────────────────────────┐
│         Simulation Orchestrator             │
│      spacecraft_simulation.py               │
└──────────────┬─────────────┬────────────────┘
               │             │
    ┌──────────┴─────┐   ┌──┴──────────┐
    │  Basilisk Core │   │ Cluster Mgr │
    │   Dynamics     │   │  Formation  │
    └────────┬───────┘   └──┬──────────┘
             │              │
    ┌────────┴──────────────┴────────┐
    │      Fault Injection Layer     │
    │  friction | power | encoder |  │
    │         battery                │
    └────────┬─────────────┬─────────┘
             │             │
    ┌────────┴─────┐   ┌──┴───────────┐
    │ ML Detection │   │ DRL Agent    │
    │  TensorFlow  │   │   PPO        │
    │              │   │  (DRL Tab)   │
    └──────┬───────┘   └──┬───────────┘
           │              │
    ┌──────┴──────────────┴─────┐
    │    Results & Plots         │
    │  Vizard | Matplotlib       │
    │     DRL Visualizations     │
    └────────────────────────────┘

Simulation Timing Note
The simulation is configured to run for 30 minutes of mission time. However, when the binary file is played back in the Vizard visualization tool, this 30-minute duration is compressed for faster playback.
In Vizard, the entire 30-minute simulation is typically displayed in about 30 seconds of real time. This time compression is intentional and allows for quick yet complete visual review of:

Reaction wheel faults
Attitude changes
Target tracking
Cluster formation dynamics
Task reassignment visualization (via DRL)
Fault detection events
Battery status changes

This compressed playback enables efficient mission analysis without waiting for full real-time duration.

